 Spatial omics data allow us to quantify various features that are related to tissue architecture. This allows us to perform comparisons of anatomical structure-derived features. We will refer to this type of analysis as **structure-based analysis**.
 
-We will use the `r BiocStyle::Biocpkg("sosta")` package to reconstruct and quantify pancreatic islets from human donors suffering different stages of diabetic type 1 (T1D) and healthy controls [@Damond2019-IMC-diabetes]. We will then compare some of the features between conditions.
